                id: "lower",
                title: "Lowering Control",
                intro: "Lower slowly and evenly, fighting the fall all the way.",
                why: "The hamstrings do their work by braking the fall. In one study, lifters who fell faster showed lower hamstring activity, and the drop usually comes as a sudden speed-up, the point where the hamstrings can no longer hold the body. Programmes that include the Nordic have about halved hamstring injuries in athletes.",
                mistake: "Letting go near the bottom and dropping the last part toward the floor.",
                correct: "Resist the whole way: lower slowly and evenly, and catch yourself on your hands only when you can no longer slow down."
